{
  "Containers that place controls: `Stack` (a row or a column), `Grid` (rows and columns), `Panel` (a plain box that can scroll), `GroupBox` (a titled frame), `DockPanel` (children stuck to its edges) and `SplitContainer` (two panes and a splitter). All of them are controls: they disable and hide what is inside, and lay out children added at any time.": "",
  "Children come as JSX or are added later with `controls.add`; either way the container picks them up. A child says where it goes in its own props (`grow`, `row`, `dock`…), whatever kind of component it is.": "",
  "Stack": "",
  "A row or a column with a gap. `align` places the children across the direction, `justify` along it; `wrap` starts a new line when they do not fit. A child with `grow` takes the free space.": "",
  "Spacing": "",
  "`gap` and `padding` take a step of the spacing scale, a number of pixels or any CSS length.": "",
  "A step of the spacing scale: `xxs`, `xs`, `sm`, `md`, `lg`, `xl`, `xxl`, from the `layout.space.*` tokens (the design system's `space.1` … `space.12`). Density and themes reach them.": "",
  "A number is pixels.": "",
  "Any CSS length.": "",
  "A padding takes one to four values, as in CSS (block-start, inline-end, block-end, inline-start), steps and lengths mixed. They follow the reading direction.": "",
  "Grid": "",
  "Rows and columns written like CSS. Children fill the cells in order, or say where they go: `row`, `column`, `rowSpan`, `columnSpan`, counted from 1.": "",
  "Tracks": "",
  "CSS grid tracks; a bare number is pixels.": "",
  "`*` is `1fr`, `2*` is `2fr`.": "",
  "Any CSS track, functions included.": "",
  "The same as a list.": "",
  "A number: that many equal columns (or rows).": "",
  "A form": "",
  "Fixed and flexible tracks": "",
  "Panel": "",
  "A plain box: padding, a frame if you want one, and its own scrolling. A scrolling panel is a Tab stop, so it can be scrolled with the keys; `text` names it.": "",
  "GroupBox": "",
  "A titled frame around related controls: a `<fieldset>`, so screen readers name the group by its title and disabling it disables what is inside. The title's `&` key focuses the first control; `collapsible` makes the title show and hide the content.": "",
  "DockPanel": "",
  "Children stick to the edges in the order they come — `top`, `bottom`, `start`, `end` (these two follow the reading direction) — and `fill` takes what is left. A `float` child sits over the rest at its own `left` / `top` / `right` / `bottom`. Laid out with CSS grid: nothing runs when the size changes.": "",
  "An app shell": "",
  "SplitContainer": "",
  "Two panes, `first` and `second`, with a splitter between them that the pointer drags and the keys move. `fixedPanel` keeps one pane's size when the container is resized; the minimum sizes hold; Enter hides the first pane and brings it back. Split containers nest.": "",
  "Nested split containers": "",
  "The splitter is one Tab stop between the panes; a scrolling `Panel` is a Tab stop of its own.": "",
  "Move the splitter by `step`; Left and Right follow what you see in a right-to-left page.": "",
  "The first pane at its smallest / largest size.": "",
  "Hides the first pane, or restores the splitter where it was.": "",
  "Focuses the first control in a `GroupBox` (Control + Option + key on Apple platforms).": "",
  "Scroll a focused scrolling `Panel`, as the browser does.": "",
  "`role=\"separator\"`, focusable, `aria-valuenow` (the first pane's share, 0–100), `aria-valuemin` / `aria-valuemax`, `aria-orientation`, `aria-controls` the first pane, named from `splitterLabel` or `uiLocale` (the ARIA window splitter pattern).": "",
  "`inert`: out of reach of Tab and screen readers; focus inside moves to the splitter.": "",
  "A native `<fieldset>`, named by its `<legend>`; disabled, it disables the native controls inside. A collapsible one has a button with `aria-expanded`.": "",
  "With `text`, a region landmark of that name. Scrolling, it is a Tab stop.": "",
  "Stack, Grid and DockPanel place children with CSS only: Tab and screen readers keep the document order, so write the children in reading order.": "",
  "The only text the containers write is the splitter's name, `uiLocale.strings.resize`, unless `splitterLabel` gives one.": "",
  "`data-orientation`, `data-align`, `data-justify`, `data-wrap`, `data-reverse`, `data-inline`; a growing child gets `data-mx-grow`.": "",
  "`data-align`, `data-justify`, `data-inline`; tracks and child places are inline grid properties.": "",
  "Each child gets `data-mx-dock`; its place and the `gap` (a margin on the side facing the rest) are inline.": "",
  "Written inline from `gap`, `rowGap`, `columnGap` (Stack, Grid, GroupBox).": "",
  "The spacing steps of `gap` and `padding`.": "",
  "The gap of Stack and Grid when none is given.": "",
  "Unit: a panel (`outline`: a frame, `card`: a raised surface).": "",
  "Units: a group box (`plain`, `collapsed`), its caption, the button that folds it and its chevron.": "",
  "The gap inside a group box when none is given; where its caption sits.": "",
  "Units: the splitter (`focus`), its line and its grip (`active`, `disabled`).": "",
  "`size` (the area that takes the pointer), `line-width`, `active-width`, `grip-length`, `grip-thickness`.": "",
  "Every container also has the shared properties of `Control`: `enabled` / `disabled` (cascading to everything inside), `visible`, `tabStop`, `tabIndex`.": "",
  "Stack props": "",
  "`horizontal` follows the reading direction.": "",
  "The space between the children.": "",
  "The space inside the edges.": "",
  "Across the direction: `start`, `center`, `end`, `stretch`, `baseline`.": "",
  "Along it: `start`, `center`, `end`, `space-between`, `space-around`, `space-evenly`.": "",
  "Children that do not fit go on to a new line.": "",
  "The children are laid out from the other end (Tab order stays the document order).": "",
  "Flows in a line of text, as wide as its children.": "",
  "Grid props": "",
  "one column": "",
  "See Grid tracks.": "",
  "Between rows and columns.": "",
  "One direction only.": "",
  "The size of tracks made as needed (a number is pixels).": "",
  "How children without a place fill the grid: `row`, `column`, `row dense`, `column dense`.": "",
  "Where children sit in their cells, up and down.": "",
  "Where children sit in their cells, along the row.": "",
  "Flows in a line of text.": "",
  "Panel props": "",
  "Scrolls its content; it is then a Tab stop, so the keys scroll it.": "",
  "`plain`, `outline` (a border), `card` (a card surface).": "",
  "Names the panel: it becomes a region landmark with that name.": "",
  "GroupBox props": "",
  "The legend; `&Address` makes Alt+A focus the first control inside. The same property as `text`.": "",
  "The title is a button that shows and hides the content.": "",
  "The content is hidden (with `collapsible`).": "",
  "The space inside the frame.": "",
  "The space between the children (they stack in a column).": "",
  "`outline` (a frame, the title on its edge) or `plain` (the title over the content).": "",
  "DockPanel props": "",
  "The space between a docked child and what it docks against.": "",
  "SplitContainer props": "",
  "`horizontal`: the panes side by side, as in Stack; `vertical`: one over the other.": "",
  "The size of the pane that keeps its size (the first one with `fixedPanel=\"none\"`): pixels, a share, a CSS length. `x-model` binds it.": "",
  "The pane that keeps its size when the container is resized. `none`: both grow, the position is kept as a share.": "",
  "The smallest size of each pane, in pixels.": "",
  "A pane that is hidden; the other takes all the room.": "",
  "The pointer and the keys move the splitter.": "",
  "Enter and a double click hide and restore the first pane.": "",
  "How far an arrow key moves the splitter, in pixels.": "",
  "The splitter's accessible name.": "",
  "Props a child gives its container": "",
  "Read by": "",
  "Takes the free space along the direction; numbers share it in proportion.": "",
  "The line it starts at, from 1 (a string goes to CSS as it is: `-1`).": "",
  "How many tracks it covers.": "",
  "`top`, `bottom`, `start`, `end`, `fill` (default) or `float`.": "",
  "The anchors of a `float` child; a number is pixels; `left` + `right` stretch it.": "",
  "The panes, two `Panel`s: `split.first.controls.add(…)`, `split.second.scrollable = true`.": "",
  "The `role=\"separator\"` element.": "",
  "`position`, for `x-model`.": "",
  "The `<legend>`.": "",
  "`void`, value": "",
  "A child's `grow` programmatically (a value or a function).": "",
  "A child's `row`, `column`, `rowSpan`, `columnSpan` programmatically.": "",
  "A child's `dock` programmatically.": "",
  "The `left` / `top` / `right` / `bottom` of a `float` child.": "",
  "Hides a pane (the first by default) / shows both again.": "",
  "Focuses the first control inside, opening a collapsed box.": "",
  "The splitter moved (at the end of a drag), or a pane was hidden or restored. `e`: `{ position, collapsed, byUser, source }`.": "",
  "The content was shown or hidden. `e`: `{ collapsed, byUser, source }`.": "",
  "`ChildSettings` — the part that reads a child's settings from its props and follows children added later — is exported for containers of your own.": ""
}
